  "claim": "John Charles Cutler was involved in observing the natural progression of untreated syphilis in rural African-American men in Alabama.",
  "evidencia": "Page: John Charles Cutler. Sentence: John Charles Cutler (June 29, 1915 – February 8, 2003) was a senior surgeon, and the acting chief of the venereal disease program in the United States Public Health Service.\nPage: Tuskegee syphilis experiment. Sentence: The Tuskegee Study of Untreated Syphilis in the Negro Male, also known as the Tuskegee Syphilis Study or Tuskegee Syphilis Experiment ( ) was an infamous clinical study conducted between 1932 and 1972 by the U.S. Public Health Service.\nPage: Tuskegee syphilis experiment. Sentence: The purpose of this study was to observe the natural progression of untreated syphilis in rural African-American men in Alabama under the guise of receiving free health care from the United States government.",
